# PART D — Windows

## D5. Shared PC mode — documented model

Canonical URLs (the ones in the brief 404; these are the live ones):
- https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/configuration/shared-pc/set-up-shared-or-guest-pc (ms.date 2024-10-31)
- https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/configuration/shared-pc/shared-pc-technical (ms.date 2024-10-31)
- https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/client-management/mdm/sharedpc-csp (ms.date 2025-03-12)

**Deletion policy (CSP, exact):**
> "DeletionPolicy — Configures when accounts will be deleted. Allowed values: 0 (delete immediately), 1 (delete at disk space threshold), 2 (Delete at disk space threshold and inactive threshold)." **Default Value: 1.**

**Storage-based cleanup (exact):**
> "DiskLevelDeletion — Accounts will start being deleted when available disk space falls below this threshold, given as percent of total disk capacity. Accounts that have been inactive the longest will be deleted first." Default **25**.
> "DiskLevelCaching — Stop deleting accounts when available disk space reaches this threshold, given as percent of total disk capacity." Default **50**.
> "For example, if the DiskLevelCaching is set to 50 and the DiskLevelDeletion is set to 25 (both default values). Accounts will be cached while the free disk space is above 25%. When the free disk space is less than 25% (the deletion number) during a daily maintenance period, accounts will be deleted (oldest last used first) when the system is idle until the free disk space is above 50% (the caching number). **Accounts will be deleted immediately on signing out from an account if free space is under half of the deletion threshold and disk space is low**, regardless of whether the PC is actively in use or not."

> "InactiveThreshold — Accounts will start being deleted when they haven't been logged-on during the specified period, given as number of days." Default **30**.
> "AccountModel — Allowed values: 0 (only guest), 1 (domain-joined only), 2 (domain-joined and guest)." Default **0**.

**What actually gets removed (exact, from set-up-shared-or-guest-pc):**
> "When a device is configured in *shared PC mode* with the default deletion policy, **accounts will be cached automatically until disk space is low**. Then, accounts will be deleted to reclaim disk space… Both Microsoft Entra ID and Active Directory domain accounts are managed in this way. **Any accounts created through Guest and Kiosk will be deleted automatically at sign out.**"
> "**Local accounts that already exist on a PC won't be deleted** when turning on shared PC mode. **New local accounts** that are created using Settings > Accounts > Other people > Add someone else to this PC after shared PC mode is turned on **won't be deleted.**"
> "The account management service supports accounts that are **exempt from deletion**… by adding the account SID to the registry key: `HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTARE\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\SharedPC\Exemptions\`" (typo "SOFTARE" is Microsoft's, verbatim in the doc).

**The load-bearing finding — Shared PC mode deliberately WEAKENS cross-user data isolation.** From the technical reference's table of LGPO settings applied by `EnableSharedPCMode`:

> "Windows Components/App Package Deployment/**Allow a Windows app to share application data between users** | **Enabled**"

Also enabled by the same switch, security-relevant: UAC "Behavior of elevation prompt for standard user → **Automatically deny elevation requests**"; "Hide entry points for Fast User Switching → Enabled"; "Allow the use of biometrics → **Disabled**"; "Allow users to log on using biometrics → **Disabled**"; "Windows Hello for Business / Use Windows Hello for Business → **Disabled**"; "Turn on convenience PIN sign-in → Disabled"; "Turn off picture password sign-in → Enabled"; "Enumerate local users on domain-joined computers → Disabled"; "Turn off File History → Enabled"; phone sign-in registry value set to 0.

`EnableAccountManager` does exactly one thing: "the following schedule task is turned on: `\Microsoft\Windows\SharedPC\Account Cleanup`". **Deletion is a scheduled maintenance task, not a sign-out guarantee** — except for Guest/Kiosk and the low-disk case.

Troubleshooting surface: `C:\Windows\SharedPCSetup.log`, `HKLM\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\SharedPC`.

**No security caveat section exists in either doc.** Microsoft nowhere states what shared PC mode does *not* isolate. That silence + the "share application data between users → Enabled" row is the whole story: Shared PC mode is a **storage-hygiene and account-lifecycle feature, not an isolation feature.**

## D6. Windows cross-account CVEs (NVD REST, keywordSearch)

